  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Saturday...\n\nUpper level ridging will prevail through at least midweek,\nbringing warm and dry conditions. High temperatures today will be\nin the low 70s to low 80s, increasing to low 80s to low 90s by \nWendesday. \n\nA disturbance moving across northern Montana late tonight through\nMonday will bring breezy winds out of the north, with widespread \ngusts of 25 to 40 mph. Given the dry and breezy conditions Monday,\nalong with highs 10 to 20 degrees above normal today and Monday, \nthere are some increased grass fire concerns, especially for areas\nnortheast of Billings. Take care not to cause a spark!\n\nThere are signs of an unsettled pattern developing the second half\nof the week. There is still significant disagreement between\nmodels, but there is moderate confidence for daily showers and\nthunderstorms to develop and highs to return to 70s and 80s.\nArcher",
